`,n(e.p,{children:"Schemas validate raw data types like strings, numbers, objects, or unions. Methods help you use or modify a schema. Actions are used inside a pipeline to validate, transform, or describe data in more detail."}),`
`,n(e.p,{children:"Once you understand these three building blocks, the rest of the library becomes much easier to reason about. This matters even more in larger codebases where schemas are shared across forms, API boundaries, workers, and internal utilities."}),`
